equal rights for all  the internet has opened new  communication channels for people with  disabilities  a german online activist shows how you  can use blogs for political agendas  porbst is at the church congress in  hamburg the hearing impaired blogger is  angry  she wants to follow a debate with german  president joachim gaok  but she can't see him from her seat  ironically the discussion is about  rights for people with disabilities  the 31 year old doesn't let up until a  new row of seats are set up for people  with hearing disabilities  it's a small victory but for julia  probst this is just one step  the blogger has an assignment the online  magazine of the dia cooney charity wants  her to examine the accessibility for the  disabled at major events  she sends her observations to around  twenty four thousand twitter followers  sometimes every five minutes  in her blog nine augenshmas or feast for  the eyes  she examines issues that are especially  important to her  the internet has drastically changed the  lives of the hearing impaired  her dedication and unpaid involvement  won her nomination for the bobs  the competition for online activism  since 2004 deutsche welle has been  honoring international bloggers with the  award  this year's prize went to chinese human  rights activist lee chen peng  julia popes was the runner-up  german journalist falk steiner convinced  many on the jury that she deserved  recognition  in germany things are improving for the  disabled but there's still a long way to  go  in many countries the disabled are shut  out they're severely disadvantaged and  at the bottom of what we call society  that's why it was important for me to  bring it to the attention of the  international jury  blogging alone is no longer enough for  julia porbst  for 10 months she's been a pirate party  candidate for upcoming elections to the  german parliament  where she hopes to fight for equal  rights for the disabled  she's seen for herself how intolerant  the world around her can be  after one tv interview she received a  lot of hate mail  much of it from people who made fun of  her voice she took a break  reconsidered her candidacy but decided  to push on  yeah the corners  you're going to perfect the ice pack  about your beautiful  dragon the election to parliament is set  for september the 22nd  it will decide if germany is ready for a  hearing impaired parliamentarian  schiff says a woman with a mission
 

